{title: King of My Heart}
{song_number: 36}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D]Let the King of my heart be the mountain [G]where I run,
the [D]fountain [Bm]I drink [A]from; oh, [G]He is my [D]song.
[D]Let the King of my heart be the shadow [G]where I hide,
the [D]ransom [Bm]for my [A]life; oh, [G]He is my [D]song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
You are [Bm]good, [Asus4]good, [G]oh. [D]You are [Bm]good, [Asus4]good, [G]oh. [D]
You are [Bm]good, [Asus4]good, [G]oh. [D]You are [G]good, [D]good, oh.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D]Let the King of my heart be the wind in[G]side my sails,
the [D]anchor [Bm]in the [A]waves; oh, [G]He is my [D]song.
[D]Let the King of my heart be the fire in[G]side my veins,
the [D]echo [Bm]of my [A]days; oh, [G]He is my [D]song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
